WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.741 --> 00:00:04.749
- [Narrator] This is a golden mantella.

00:00:04.749 --> 00:00:06.051
They're critically endangered

00:00:06.051 --> 00:00:07.587
and only found in a mere four square miles

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:10.504
in part of east central Madagascar.

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:17.037
At only one inch long, this little one

00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:19.384
is actually fully grown,

00:00:19.384 --> 00:00:23.437
but what they may lack in size
they make up for in color.

00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:25.485
Their mildly toxic skin is bright yellow,

00:00:25.485 --> 00:00:27.652
orange, and sometimes red.

00:00:28.835 --> 00:00:30.562
Golden mantellas are insectivores,

00:00:30.562 --> 00:00:32.376
feeding on termites, fruit flies,

00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:35.427
and a range of other insects.

00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:37.475
Although they have very
few predators in the wild,

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:41.741
they've been over-collected
for the pet trade.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.517
They're endemic to swamps with
elevations close to 3,000 feet

00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:47.906
but rapid deforestation
of their unique habitat

00:00:47.906 --> 00:00:50.906
has left them critically endangered.

00:00:52.024 --> 00:00:54.441
This is the golden mantella.

